package CanvasNet {
    part def FeatureCatalog {
        doc /* The internal static FeatureCatalog with the FeatureReport record and the FeatureReportKind enumeration: a pure function of the parsed SpecTree that lists every construct of a Vega-Lite specification that the renderer recognizes but does not implement, each with a stable lower-case vl- identifier (vl-schema-version, vl-data-*, vl-mark-type, vl-channel-name, vl-type-*, vl-scale-*, vl-encoding-*, vl-guide-*, vl-format-type-custom, vl-expr-*, vl-transform-name, vl-composition-*, vl-param-*, vl-projection, vl-layout-autosize-*) and the exact location, sorted by line and column with a stable sort. Phase 5 removes the reports of the supported expressions and transforms (vl-expr-calculate, vl-expr-filter, and vl-transform-calculate, filter, fold, flatten, sample, pivot, and lookup of the drawn view, vl-param-variable of the drawn view, and vl-expr-ref at the row-bound sites) and adds vl-expr-function-name (a function outside the whitelist, the name lower-cased in the identifier and as written in the message), vl-expr-view-state (signal, event, item, and undeclared width, height, padding, autosize, background, or cursor), vl-expr-construct-name (bitwise and shift operators and in), each at the expression string with the offset in the message, plus vl-transform-filter-param, vl-transform-filter-timeunit, vl-transform-filter-datetime, vl-transform-pivot-op, and vl-transform-lookup-param for the parts of supported transforms that are not executed; Phase 6 removes the reports of the supported grouping transforms and encodings (vl-transform-aggregate, joinaggregate, window, bin, stack, and impute of the drawn view, vl-encoding-aggregate, vl-encoding-stack, vl-encoding-bin of x and y, vl-scale-bin-ordinal, vl-encoding-sort of the supported forms, vl-channel-x2 and vl-channel-y2 of bar, rect, and rule marks, and vl-channel-order when it orders an active stack, decided with the StackRules of the Transforms subsystem) and adds vl-encoding-bin-extent-param and vl-transform-bin-extent-param (an extent given by a parameter, ignored) and vl-encoding-stack-nonlinear (an explicit stack on a scale that is not linear); the transforms timeunit, regression, loess, density, quantile, and extent, every transform and variable parameter of a nested view, the encoding impute (vl-encoding-impute), selection parameters, conditional encodings (vl-encoding-condition), bin: "binned" on a channel other than x and y and a bin of order or a secondary channel (vl-encoding-bin), and the channel sorts that are not ascending, descending, null, a value list, an encoding sort, or an aggregate object (vl-encoding-sort) stay reported. The Step 0 sort diagnostics refine the channel sorts: a sort that refers to a channel the encoding lacks is vl-encoding-sort with a message that names the channel, and a sort array, channel, or object on a quantitative field with a continuous scale is the warning vl-encoding-sort-ignored. Phase 7 (colors and channels) removes vl-scale-color-ramp (retired: continuous colors are drawn), the reports of the scale types sequential, quantile, quantize, and threshold and of the scale properties domainMid, domainMin, domainMax, rangeMin, rangeMax, and interpolate, the report of an unavailable scheme (an unknown scheme is a specification error), and vl-channel-shape, vl-channel-strokewidth, vl-channel-strokedash, vl-channel-fillopacity, vl-channel-strokeopacity, and vl-channel-angle for the marks that draw them (shape, angle, and strokeDash stay reported and ignored on a mark that does not draw them), and adds vl-scale-interpolate-cubehelix, vl-shape-path (a custom SVG path shape, drawn as a circle), and the warning vl-scale-type-ignored (a scale type that the channel or field type cannot use, and a quantitative field on shape or strokeDash). The log-family scales remove the reports of the scale types log, pow, sqrt, and symlog and of the scale properties base, exponent, and constant (vl-encoding-stack-nonlinear stays for an explicit stack on a scale that is not linear, and its message says that the marks of a log, pow, sqrt, or symlog scale are not stacked). It is the single definition of the supported boundary: supported marks, channels, scale types, scale properties, and data sources are absent from its result. It classifies a data url as remote (a scheme, drive letter, absolute path, or network path: vl-data-remote-url, never fetched; a relative local path is supported and not reported), reports a custom parse date format as vl-data-parse-date-format and text or object datasets as vl-data-values-text or vl-data-geo, chooses a data source by precedence rather than key order, and reports an empty or sourceless data object as the warning vl-data-empty; it opens no file, reads no data rows, and uses no network. The identifiers vl-data-file, vl-data-named, vl-data-sequence, vl-data-parse, vl-data-format-*, and vl-data-property are retired (their constructs are supported). The warnings vl-duplicate-key, vl-unknown-property, and vl-encoding-sort-mixed-types are produced by the SpecParser unit. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/FeatureCatalog.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/FeatureCatalogTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/feature-catalog.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/feature-catalog.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/feature-catalog.yaml */
    }
}
